      "id": "sol.amc-8-1988-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Adding, \\(\\dfrac{1}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{6} + \\dfrac{2}{6} = \\dfrac{5}{6}.\\)\n\nThe reciprocal of \\(\\dfrac{5}{6}\\) is \\(\\dfrac{6}{5}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "First add the fractions using a common denominator of \\(6\\)",
        "The reciprocal flips the numerator and denominator"
